# Own-wording spells of Artificer Expansion Pack (2024). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Artifice Overcharge": ["Level 5. A magic item explodes in a 30 ft Emanation for 10d6 Force (Dex save halves) and pushes creatures 10 ft. You can drain the item's magic for a turn.",
 "Range 90 ft. Pick a magic item you see. Each creature in a 30 ft Emanation centered on it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 10d6 Force damage and is pushed 10 ft away from the item. On a success it takes half damage only. A creature holding or wearing the item has Disadvantage on the save. On a fail it drops the item if held, or has the Prone condition if worn. You can also make an ability check with your spellcasting modifier to drain the item. On a success it becomes a mundane version of itself until the start of your next turn. The DC depends on rarity. Common 8, Uncommon 11, Rare 14, Very Rare 17, Legendary 20."],
"Automation Barrage": ["Level 3. Three spectral automata attack creatures you see. Ranged spell attack, 2d4 + casting modifier Force, and each attached automaton gives -1 AC and -1 to attacks.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 round. Three tiny spectral automata fly at creatures you see in range. Make a ranged spell attack against each target, all at the same time. On a hit the target takes Force damage equal to 2d4 plus your spellcasting modifier, and the automaton latches on. The target takes a -1 penalty to AC and to attack rolls for each automaton attached to it. The automata vanish at the start of your next turn. **Higher Levels.** You conjure one more automaton for each slot level above 3."],
"Automate": ["Level 3, 1 minute. Program one action into an object that fires when a trigger you name occurs. Lasts 24 hours.",
 "Touch an object not already under this spell and program one action into it. When the trigger you set at the end of the casting occurs, the object springs to life, performs the action, and the spell ends. The action must relate directly to how the object is used and take no more than one action. Usually this is Utilize for mundane objects or Magic for magic items, at the DM's discretion. The object can move up to 5 ft as part of it. The action cannot involve an attack roll. If it needs an ability check, roll it with your own ability score. The action runs the moment the trigger occurs, whether you want it or not. For example, a potion could give itself to its carrier when that creature drops to 0 Hit Points. You can choose to consume the material component (silicon worth 500+ GP). If you do, the duration becomes until dispelled and the spell does not end when the action runs. The action cannot trigger again for 6 seconds. The spell ends early if the object gets more than 10 ft from where it was when you cast the spell."],
"Dynamo Swarm": ["Level 4, Concentration, 10 minutes. A 10 ft Sphere of tiny automatons. Each turn as a Bonus Action, move it 30 ft and Dismantle (4d8 Force, Con save halves), Relocate, or Retroflection (Invisible).",
 "Range 60 ft. You deploy a swarm of tiny flying automatons at a point in range. It fills a 10 ft diameter Sphere that can overlap creatures. When you create it and as a Bonus Action on your later turns, you can move it up to 30 ft and give it one command. **Dismantle.** Creatures and objects in the area make a Constitution save. On a fail they take 4d8 Force damage, or half on a success. Constructs and objects take double. **Relocate.** The swarm picks up every Medium or smaller creature and object in its area and carries them to a new spot on the ground within 20 ft. The swarm moves with them. An unwilling creature can resist with a Strength save. **Retroflection.** The automatons show the scenery behind them until the end of your next turn. A creature fully inside the area in that time has the Invisible condition. **Higher Levels.** With a level 5+ slot the Sphere is 15 ft in diameter."],
"Elemental Strikes": ["Level 1 Bonus Action, Concentration, 1 minute. A willing creature's Unarmed Strikes deal a chosen elemental type, use a d8, and add 1d6 once per turn.",
 "Touch a willing creature and pick Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. For the duration its Unarmed Strikes deal that damage type, and it can roll a d8 instead of the normal Unarmed Strike damage. The first time it hits with an Unarmed Strike on each turn, that hit deals an extra 1d6 damage. **Higher Levels.** The extra damage is 2d6 with a level 3 or 4 slot and 3d6 with a level 5+ slot."],
"Fall Loop": ["Level 1. A creature in range that is not flying makes a Dex save or falls 30 ft through a portal loop and takes falling damage.",
 "Range 60 ft. You open two linked portals for a moment, one right under a creature you see and one just above it. If the creature is not flying it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it falls through the portals in a loop for 30 ft, then the portals vanish and it lands in its original space and takes falling damage. **Higher Levels.** The fall is 20 ft longer for each slot level above 1."],
"Imbue Sentience": ["Level 5, 8 hours. Give a non-sentient object of Large or smaller size awareness, or move a willing soul into it. Consumes a sapphire worth 1,000+ GP.",
 "Touch a non-sentient object that is Large or smaller and is not a creature's remains. It gains sentience, with Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma of 10 and the ability to speak one language you know. As an alternative, when the casting ends you can move the soul of a free and willing creature within 5 ft of you (or its corpse) into the object. The creature must be alive or have died within the last 24 hours. The soul stays in the object for good. The object takes the creature's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma and knows its languages. A living creature's body dies at once and cannot be revived while the soul is in the object. If the object is destroyed, the soul is freed and goes to its afterlife. You decide these things when you finish. **Personality.** If the mind is not from a creature, you set its personality, allegiances, and knowledge, which cannot exceed your own. After the casting the DM controls it and it can change like any creature. **Speech.** It speaks as if it had a mouth, or only to creatures touching it. **Movement.** If the object has moving parts you can let it move them, with Strength and Dexterity of 10. Otherwise it cannot move."],
"Instant Barricade": ["Level 3, 10 minutes. Create a fixed barricade up to a 10 ft Cube with the Instant Barricade stat block. You pick its look.",
 "Range 60 ft. You create a barricade no larger than a 10 ft Cube in an open space in range. It stays fixed for the duration or until destroyed. You choose its look, size, and shape, and whether it is opaque or clear. Whatever you choose, it uses the Instant Barricade stat block. **Higher Levels.** Use the slot level as the spell level in the stat block. The Cube is 5 ft larger for each slot level above 3."],
"Magnet Trap": ["Level 2, Concentration, 1 minute. A magnet with a 10 ft radius Sphere pulls Tiny metal objects and slows metal creatures (Str save).",
 "Range 30 ft. A powerful magnet appears at a point you see and attracts metal in a 10 ft radius Sphere. Tiny metal objects there that nobody wears or carries fly to the center. When a creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it makes a Strength save. On a fail it has Disadvantage on attacks with metal weapons until the start of its next turn. Also on a fail, a creature made of metal or wearing metal armor cannot move away from the center until the start of its next turn. On a success, the creature must still spend twice the movement to move away while in the area. **Higher Levels.** The radius is 5 ft bigger for each slot level above 2."],
"Protective Gizmo": ["Level 1, 1 hour. A willing creature gets a gizmo for one ability. The first failed save with it is rerolled and the new roll is used.",
 "Touch a willing creature and build a magic machine for it from gears and springs. Pick one ability when you cast the spell. The first time the target fails a saving throw with that ability before the spell ends, the gizmo fires and protects it. The target rerolls the save and must use the new roll. Then the gizmo falls apart and the spell ends. **Higher Levels.** The gizmo can fire once more without ending the spell for each slot level above 1."],
"Railgun": ["Level 3. Fire ammunition in a 100 ft Line, 5 ft wide, for 4d12 Piercing (Dex save halves). It ignores Cover but panels of force stop it.",
 "You fire the material component (a piece of ammunition) from a Ranged weapon you hold that can use it. It flies in a 100 ft Line that is 5 ft wide. It pierces creatures and objects, including Cover, but panels of force such as Wall of Force block it. Creatures and objects in the line take 4d12 Piercing damage. An unwilling creature makes a Dexterity save to take half damage on a success. If the ammunition is a magic item, creatures that fail the save are affected as if the ammunition hit them. **Higher Levels.** The damage rises by 1d12 for each slot level above 3. With a level 5+ slot the ammunition passes through panels of force."],
"Regenerating Ward": ["Level 2, Concentration, 1 minute. A willing creature gets +1 AC and gains 2 + your spellcasting modifier Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of its turns.",
 "Range 30 ft. You wrap one willing creature you see in a regenerating force field. For the duration it gains a +1 bonus to AC. At the start of each of its turns it gains Temporary Hit Points equal to 2 plus your spellcasting ability modifier. These Temporary Hit Points vanish when the spell ends. **Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Sever Attunement": ["Level 4. A creature you see makes a Cha save or its Attunement to a chosen magic item ends. Curses are not removed.",
 "Range 60 ft. You try to cut the magic link between a creature you see in range and a magic item you choose. The target makes a Charisma save. On a fail its Attunement to the item ends at once and it loses all benefits from that Attunement, though curses are not removed. If the creature is not attuned to the item, or the item is cursed so that Attunement cannot end, the spell fails and nothing happens."],
"Suppress Enchantment": ["Level 2, Concentration, 1 minute. Turn a non-Artifact magic item you see into a mundane copy. Rarer items need a spellcasting check.",
 "Range 30 ft. You try to suppress the magic of one magic item you see that is not an Artifact. A suppressed item acts as a mundane version of itself for the duration. Common and Uncommon items are suppressed with no roll. For rarer items you make an ability check with your spellcasting modifier against a DC set by rarity. Rare 15, Very Rare 18, Legendary 21. **Higher Levels.** You suppress rarer items automatically. Rare with a level 3 slot, Very Rare with level 4, and Legendary with level 5+."],
"Switch Attunement": ["Level 3 Ritual, 1 minute. Move a creature's Attunement to a different unattuned magic item, or make two creatures swap one item each.",
 "Touch a willing creature during the casting and shift its Attunement from one magic item to another item that nobody is attuned to. Its Attunement to the first item ends at once, it loses that item's Attunement benefits (curses are not removed), and it becomes attuned to the new item. As an alternative you can target two willing creatures and have them swap Attunement to one magic item each in the same way. If the original item is cursed so that Attunement cannot end, the spell fails. **Higher Levels.** The casting time is an action with a level 4 slot and a Bonus Action with a level 5+ slot."],
"System Surge": ["Level 5, Concentration, 1 minute. Your magic items use Bonus Actions, may keep charges (1d4, a 4 saves them), and use your spell save DC if higher.",
 "You supercharge your link to your magic items for the duration. You can take a Magic action granted by a magic item as a Bonus Action instead. When you spend one or more charges of a magic item, roll 1d4. On a 4 the charges are not spent. When you use a magic item that makes creatures roll a saving throw, the DC becomes your spell save DC unless it is already higher."],
"Ward Object": ["Level 2 Ritual, 8 hours. A Tiny or Small object gets Immunity to all damage, cannot be defaced, and cannot be forced from your possession.",
 "Touch a Tiny or Small object and protect it. For the duration it has Immunity to all damage and cannot be defaced in any way. It also cannot be taken from you by force. **Higher Levels.** Larger objects can be targeted. Medium with a level 3+ slot, Large with level 4+, and Huge with level 5+."],
}
